> A hand-checkable calculation

Zero weights give four equal logits and probability1/4 per action. The real experiment below initializes nonzero weights; its stopped batch-mean baseline and entropy objective stay visible.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/contextual_bandit_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace f=dm::rl::foundations;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");auto path=f::TanhCategoricalPolicy(dm::nn::zeros({1,8}),dm::nn::zeros({8,32}),dm::nn::zeros({32}),dm::nn::zeros({32,4}),dm::nn::zeros({4}));auto p=dm::nn::exp(path.log_probability).to_vector<double>();std::vector<double>values=p;for(double v:p)if(std::abs(v-.25)>1e-7)return 1;std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");for(size_t i=0;i<values.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,values[i]);dm::nn::save_npz("build/contextual_bandit_worked.npz",{{"values",dm::nn::from_vector(values)}});std::vector<double>x(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);double low=std::min(0.,*std::min_element(values.begin(),values.end())),high=std::max(0.,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.end())),span=std::max(1.,high-low);dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(x,values,"worked values",{37,99,235}).ylim(low-.05*span,high+.05*span).title("contextual bandit worked calculation").x_label("Displayed coordinate").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/contextual_bandit_worked.svg");}
