> Inspect the actual experiment results

The plot uses the original1000-round expectation windows, not Bernoulli sample rewards. Oracle is an upper benchmark with full knowledge of the current context. Greedy evaluation differs from the sampled training policy.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/contextual_bandit_results.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto archive=dm::nn::load_npz("build/contextual_bandit_source.npz");auto get=[&](const std::string& name){auto it=std::find_if(archive.begin(),archive.end(),[&](const auto& p){return p.first==name;});if(it==archive.end())throw std::runtime_error("missing source series "+name);return it->second.to_vector<double>();};auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();{auto values=get("policy");std::vector<double>x;x.resize(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),1.);plot.lines(x,values,"policy",{37,99,235});}{auto values=get("greedy");std::vector<double>x;x.resize(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),1.);plot.lines(x,values,"greedy",{234,88,12});}{auto values=get("oracle");std::vector<double>x;x.resize(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),1.);plot.lines(x,values,"oracle",{22,163,74});}{auto values=get("random");std::vector<double>x;x.resize(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),1.);plot.lines(x,values,"random",{147,51,234});}plot.title("contextual bandit source results").x_label("Source1000-round window index").y_label("Mean expected reward").size(1150,650).save_svg("build/contextual_bandit_results.svg");}
```
